-- title:
--   Reflection transports the exceptional support
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Let $p:G\to G$ be additive with $p^2=p$ and $3p(x)=0$ for every $x$. If $a,d,h\in G$ satisfy $p(a)=p(h)=0$ and $p(d)=-2d$, its associated three-reflection sends source support to target support: $$r_p(S(a,d,h))=T(a,d,h).$$ No nonzero or half-turn assumption on $h$ occurs here. Here $S(a,d,h)=\{a,a+d,a+d+h\}$ and $T(a,d,h)=\{a,a-d,a-d+h\}$; $A_U$ denotes the rational directed Cayley adjacency matrix of $U$.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L358-L384, lines 358–384; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeReflection_support

